  "body": "## Scientific scope (independent draft, 2026-10-16 KST)\n\nAdditive research on verified **PR #153** parent `e98d30efb5e725a79743d3a8ff61ee7e5169b498`; preserves PR #152 Verner donor/geodesic inputs. Separate from PR #150 native FLRW production, PR #154 C16B source owner, v3/rux DAG and all running NCP jobs/checkpoints. **Do not merge into production without a verified native adapter.**\n\n## Implemented, actually run in ChatGPT execution container\n\n1. Coupled photoionization HI\u2192HII, HeI\u2192HeII\u2192HeIII and reverse recombination HII\u2192HI, HeII\u2192HeI, HeIII\u2192HeII using **positive exact two-stock pair reaction maps** and symmetric photo\u2013recomb\u2013photo Strang splitting; Ray energies follow existing exact non-tilted LRS Bianchi I characteristics.\n2. Thermal energy `U_th=(3/2) k_B T (H_total+He_total+n_e)`, chemical binding storage, radiation redshift/shear work, gas adiabatic work, and escaped recombination energy tracked independently. Exact continuous symbolic cancellation: Wolfram Language `energy_ledger_identity=0`; isolated recombination preserves T at constant geometry with the specified thermal-electron removal closure.\n3. Recombination coefficients and rate powers are **toy normalized constants**, not physically certified Case-B rate fits. Recombination radiative energy `E_i+(3/2)k_B T` per event is a simplified escape closure; this is NOT a native EoR or actual species thermal-history prediction.\n4. **98/98 pytest passed** in independent ChatGPT Python 3.13.5 / NumPy2.3.5 / SciPy1.17.0 / pytest9.0.2. Independent continuous SciPy Radau RHS and `max_step={.08,.04,.02,.01,.005}` convergence in three signed-shear sectors. `max_step=.005` electrons and T[K] at s/H=-.04, 0, +.04: (0.07491382090756712,6368.972438), (0.07491323590241768,6369.389164), (0.0749137414064937,6368.947747); maximum mixed-state/energy differences versus Radau ~4.27\u20134.51e-6.\n5. 15-row convergence JSON, 3 signed-shear ion/temperature histories CSV, four history PNG in complete ZIP. Source donor and exact checksums preserved. All published source files, evidence, Korean mathematical report and NCP handoff can be read at `research/lrs_threshold_oracle_20261015/`.\n6. Portable `NCP_RUN_V4.sh`: source/donor SHA gate; 98 tests; Radau experiment; 12-case serial-vs-4-worker byte-identity smoke; 816-case (17 shear \u00d7 4 photo \u00d7 4 recomb \u00d7 3 initial T) two-step parallel sweep, 12 workers default / 16 max, timeout 900 s. **Runner smoke actually PASS** in the ChatGPT container. 816-case NCP sweep is NOT_RUN.\n\n## Execution / delivery scope\n\nUser Ubuntu Remote Desktop Commander is exhausted at monthly quota, **so no new Ubuntu/NCP V4 run**. No attempts to reconnect. Hand off exact user-authorized SSH `ssh -i /home/cosmosapjw/.ssh/ncp_key root@49.50.142.2 -p 22` to local Codex, with create-only NCP folder and no interference to active production jobs. See `CODEX_NCP_HANDOFF_20261016.md`, `RESEARCH_V4_KO.md`, `V4_RELEASE_MANIFEST.json`, `V4_INPUT_SHA256SUMS.txt`.\n\nPublication correction preserved: an initial GitHub source upload temporarily stored a files.read error message in `recomb_thermal.py`. That defect was **repaired** by a source-exact follow-on commit; final Git blob matches tested 11,571-byte file. CSV CRLF normalization likewise was corrected and the Git blob matches the original deterministic raw output. Do not claim the interim commits were executable.\n\n## Claim gate\n\n- Analytic source-free energy identity: **derived + Wolfram-checked**.\n- Coupled toy solver and independent Radau references: **sandbox numerically checked**.\n- Source-native physical Case-B cooling and explicit recombination photon transport: **NOT_IMPLEMENTED**.\n- User Ubuntu and NCP runtime of new V4: **NOT_RUN**.\n- Full physical EoR and PR150 native merge: **HOLD**.\n\nNCP verification and two-cloud readback are the next execution tasks; the user requested a copyable Codex handoff if remote control is unavailable.",
